/T (input\(\) always returns str. int\(\) and float\(\) convert valid numeric strings. 'eight' raises ValueError; '8,5' is not accepted by float in this locale-independent format; spaces around '8.5' are accepted after strip \(and float also accepts surrounding whitespace\). A try/except ValueError is clearer and catches malformed values without fragile string checks. Formatting {amount:8.2f} reserves width 8 and prints two decimals.)
