605 0 obj
<<
/Title (Assumptions: the rate formula is linear around the reference values; each 0.1% difference is one step; the nearest whole step is used; accepted entries are grouped by farmer and ten-day period; invalid entries are rejected and not included.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 511 0 R
/Prev 667 0 R
/Next 547 0 R
>>
endobj
606 0 obj
<<
/Title (Division / returns a float; // floors toward negative infinity \(so -7//2 is -4\); % returns the remainder. A bool is a logical value, a string stores text, and a list stores multiple values.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 548 0 R
/Next 668 0 R
>>
endobj
607 0 obj
<<
/Title (Alternative: Integer paise: convert each amount to paise and add ints; exact and O\(n\) time. Decimal: exact decimal arithmetic and O\(n\) time. Float with rounding: faster in many cases but can still accumulate errors. sys.getsizeof\(\) can measure the object size on the local Python installation; sizes are implementation-dependent.)
