/Title (Floating representation explains the first result. round\(\) chooses the nearest step; int\(\) truncates toward zero; floor\(\) moves down to the next integer. Comparison chaining is equivalent to two comparisons joined by and. Boolean operators are and, or, not.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 672 0 R
/Prev 707 0 R
/Next 708 0 R
>>
endobj
715 0 obj
<<
/Title (input\(\) always returns str. int\(\) and float\(\) convert valid numeric strings. 'eight' raises ValueError; '8,5' is not accepted by float in this locale-independent format; spaces around '8.5' are accepted after strip \(and float also accepts surrounding whitespace\). A try/except ValueError is clearer and catches malformed values without fragile string checks. Formatting {amount:8.2f} reserves width 8 and prints two decimals.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 709 0 R
/Next 716 0 R
>>
endobj
716 0 obj
<<
/Title (Alternative: String checks are fast but incomplete for signs, decimal points and whitespace. try/except costs O\(1\) for each normal entry; invalid inputs incur exception overhead. Both are O\(1\) per entry, but conversion with exception handling is more robust.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 709 0 R
/Prev 715 0 R
>>
endobj
