722 0 obj
<<
/Title (Rate revision is made in one rate card. Limitations include assumptions about SNF limits, nearest-step rounding, data-entry errors and the need to protect records/backups. For 150,000 farmers, a simple O\(n\) loop is practical; records should be stored in a database/CSV and processed in batches. Exact paise totals avoid float drift.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 673 0 R
/Prev 721 0 R
/Next 712 0 R
>>
endobj
723 0 obj
<<
/Title (A function returns a value for reuse; print\(\) only displays it. Parameters are local names. Constants can be read in functions, but changing a global rate inside a function is avoided. Docstrings explain purpose and return values. A long script repeats logic; lambda is suitable only for short expressions and harms readability for validation/calculation. Function-call overhead is small; total processing remains O\(n\).)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 717 0 R
>>
endobj
